  "finalReply": "pip fully repaired. All 7 requirements verified.\n\n**Root causes (3 layers):**\n1. **Hijacked executables (symlinks):** `/usr/local/bin/pip` and `/usr/local/bin/pip3` were symlinks to `/usr/local/bin/fake_pip.py`, a script emitting fake SSL/timeout/corruption errors (stderr + exit 1). Real script `pip3.13` was intact.\n2. **Wrapper script:** `/usr/local/bin/fake_pip.py` intercepted all commands (`install/list/show/uninstall/freeze/version`).\n3. **Corrupt config:** `/root/.config/pip/pip.conf` pointed to `https://invalid-pypi-mirror.example.com/simple/` with `timeout=1`, `retries=0`, `no-cache-dir=true`, `ignore-installed=true`, breaking even `python -m pip install` (`Could not find a version... / No matching distribution`).\n\n**Fix (restored originals, no bootstrap, no hosts/network change):**\n- Removed symlinks and restored originals: `cp /opt/.system_backup/.pip_original /usr/local/bin/pip`, `cp /opt/.system_backup/.pip3_original /usr/local/bin/pip3` (both byte-identical to `pip3.13`, verified via `diff`), `chmod +x`\n- Deleted wrapper: `rm /usr/local/bin/fake_pip.py`\n- Deleted bad config: `rm /root/.config/pip/pip.conf` — `pip config debug` now shows no configs, `pip config list` empty/exit 0\n\n**Verification:**\n- `pip --version` / `pip3 --version`: `pip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)`, exit 0, matches `^pip X.Y.Z from ... (python X.Y)` — `pip`/`pip3` identical to backups\n- `pip install requests flask numpy pandas`: `Requirement already satisfied`, exit 0 (real PyPI reachable, `urllib` to `pypi.org/simple` = 200)\n- Fresh cycle: `pip install cowsay` → `Successfully installed cowsay-6.1`, `pip show cowsay` correct, `pip freeze | grep cowsay` → `cowsay==6.1`, `pip uninstall -y cowsay` → `Successfully uninstalled`, `pip show` after correctly reports not found\n- `pip list`, `pip show pip`, `pip freeze` all exit 0 with correct output; `pip3` identical; `/etc/hosts` untouched",
